{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Is this not that in which my master drinks.</b> The meaning is: this that you took is that in which my master drinks. And he framed them with the goblet in order to magnify their guilt, for one who steals a cup from the king's house — does he not disgrace the kingdom, and is he not liable to death?" "<b>And he divines with it.</b> That is to say: you should have thought that he would inquire of diviners concerning this, and would know that you stole it. And with these words he gave a reason for why he pursued them more than all who came there from other lands — because he knew this through the art of divination, that they had stolen it. And they answered:"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:08.262466675Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}